"""Forty original robotics questions; the first choice is correct."""
RAW = '''
A programmable machine that can perform actions in the physical world is commonly called a|robot|spreadsheet cell|document title|password|A robot is a programmable machine capable of physical actions.
A robot does not have to|look like a human|have a physical effect|follow a design|use energy|Robots can take many forms and need not be human-shaped.
A factory arm following fixed programmed movements can be|a robot without machine learning|only a text file|necessarily conscious|a human operator|A robot can follow fixed instructions without machine learning.
An AI text classifier without physical actuators|can exist without being a physical robot|must be a robot|must have wheels|is a motor by definition|AI software can process data without controlling a physical machine.
A robot component that detects a condition is a|sensor|actuator|printer tray|file extension|A sensor detects or measures a condition.
A component that turns a command into physical movement is an|actuator|email address|worksheet|webpage|An actuator produces physical action.
The component that processes input and directs action is the|controller|paper clip|desk surface|monitor stand|A controller applies instructions and sends commands.
A distance sensor can provide information about|how far away an obstacle is|the licence of a photograph|the colour of a paper folder only|a spreadsheet password|A distance sensor measures or estimates distance.
A light sensor detects|light|the number of printed pages by definition|the legal owner of a file|a user's job title|A light sensor detects light.
A temperature sensor measures|temperature|software licence terms|a flowchart's title|the size of a word-processing font|A temperature sensor detects or measures temperature.
A touch sensor can report|physical contact|a network password|the result of every arithmetic question|the contents of a licence automatically|A touch sensor detects physical contact or related pressure.
A camera can provide a controller with|image data|guaranteed correct object labels without processing|physical torque directly|a permanent backup by definition|A camera captures images; interpretation requires suitable processing.
A motor rotating a wheel is functioning as an|actuator|email attachment|input document|text paragraph|A motor produces physical motion and is an actuator.
A gripper mechanism moves an object. Its movement is|physical action|a spreadsheet formula|a licence condition|a web address|A gripper acts physically on an object.
A robot's power supply provides|energy|the correct answer to every question|legal permission to enter any site|a guarantee against faults|The power supply provides energy to system components.
A controller's output can be sent to|an actuator|only a paper notebook|only a screen frame|no component|The controller may command an actuator to perform an action.
In a simple obstacle-avoidance robot, a distance measurement is|input to the control process|the same as the motor's physical rotation|a printed result necessarily|an intellectual-property licence|A sensor measurement provides information to the controller.
In the same robot, turning a wheel is|an action performed by an actuator|a character encoding|a privacy notice|a file backup|Wheel movement is physical action generated by an actuator.
Feedback provides information about|an outcome that can guide subsequent control|only the robot's name|only the colour of a diagram|only a file extension|Feedback reports an outcome for use in later control.
A system adjusts a motor using measured position. It uses|feedback control|only manual filing|no information about its outcome|a word-processing function|The measured position is feedback used to adjust control.
A timer runs a motor for a fixed duration without measuring the result. This is an example of|open-loop control|closed-loop position feedback|a spreadsheet formula|data encryption|The action is not adjusted using feedback about the controlled outcome.
A controller measures temperature and adjusts a heater using that measurement. This is an example of|closed-loop control|only paper storage|a keyboard shortcut|a text encoding|The measured temperature is feedback for the controller.
Open-loop control in the relevant loop|does not use outcome feedback to adjust the action|always uses position feedback|guarantees perfect performance|cannot use electricity|Open-loop control does not use feedback about the controlled outcome to adjust that loop.
Closed-loop control in the relevant loop|uses feedback about the outcome|cannot contain a sensor|guarantees safety in every design|uses no control rule|Closed-loop control uses measured outcome feedback.
Whether a robot is safe depends on|its design, environment, safeguards and use|only whether it resembles a person|only its name|whether it has a blue case|Safety depends on the specific system and its context.
A possible industrial robot safeguard is|guarding and an appropriate emergency stop|assuming the machine can never malfunction|entering a hazardous area during operation without permission|removing all maintenance|Guarding and emergency stops are examples of safety measures where appropriate.
An obstacle sensor gives a wrong reading. A robot may|respond incorrectly unless safeguards handle the fault|automatically become conscious|always repair itself|prove all sensors are infallible|Sensor errors can lead to incorrect behaviour and require appropriate handling.
Robots are used in some warehouses to|transport items|guarantee no worker ever needs training|eliminate all safety procedures|replace all data|Some robots transport items within warehouse environments.
An industrial arm repeating a welding movement demonstrates|a programmed physical action|a text-only calculation necessarily|a file extension|a network address|A robot arm can perform a programmed physical task.
A robot inspecting a hazardous area can|reduce some human exposure when properly used|guarantee all risks disappear|make safeguards unnecessary|be assumed reliable without testing|Robots can help reduce exposure, but risk and reliability still matter.
A controller should turn a heater on when the temperature is below 18. At 17, the condition is|true|false|a filename|a printer|Seventeen is below eighteen, so the stated condition is true.
A controller should turn a heater on when the temperature is below 18. At 18, the condition is|false|true|a physical cable|a backup|The condition is strictly below 18 and does not include 18.
A controller should turn a heater on when the temperature is at most 18. At 18, the condition is|true|false|a document title|a keyboard|At most 18 includes the boundary value 18.
Which pair correctly matches component and function?|sensor measures; actuator acts|sensor acts; actuator stores passwords only|controller is always a paper tray|motor measures text grammar|A sensor detects conditions and an actuator produces action.
A robot with several sensors|can combine different inputs according to its design|must always have only one actuator|cannot have a controller|is necessarily a human being|Robot designs can use multiple sensors and actuators.
A communication link on a robot can|allow exchange of data|guarantee every message is safe|replace all sensors by definition|eliminate the need for power|A communication link can exchange information with other systems.
A robot's controller applies|instructions or a control procedure|only an unexamined legal assumption|a paper clip|a desk colour|The controller uses instructions and available inputs to direct action.
A robot may need maintenance because|components and software can develop faults|robots cannot wear or fail|maintenance is never relevant to machines|all sensors are always accurate|Physical and software faults can occur and require maintenance.
A camera image becomes an object label when|suitable processing interprets the image|a camera is present regardless of processing|the monitor is turned off|the image is renamed|Capturing an image and interpreting it are different operations.
Which statement about robotics and AI is sound?|some robots use AI, but robotics and AI are not identical|every robot uses machine learning|every AI program is a physical robot|a robot must resemble a human|Robots may use AI, but each field can exist without the other.
'''
ITEMS = []
for line in RAW.strip().splitlines():
    stem, correct, wrong1, wrong2, wrong3, explanation = line.split('|')
    ITEMS.append((stem, (correct, wrong1, wrong2, wrong3), explanation))
